<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- MATCHED CONTROL FOR ARM C - "C-random-pool", DRAW r6, SEED 44

     This is the control that actually isolates arm C's optimiser.

     The bounding-box control (batch_params_2026_CR{1,2,3}_seed*.xml) draws the
     ten new sites uniformly from street nodes across the whole demand bounding
     box. That box is several times the area of the demand footprint, so that arm
     differs from arm C in TWO ways at once - where it looks AND how it chooses.

     This arm holds the SEARCH SPACE identical. The ten sites are drawn at random
     from EXACTLY the 498-node candidate set arm C's greedy capacity-aware
     p-median searched, rebuilt verbatim from build_scenario_c_2026.py (600 m grid
     dedup of street nodes in the demand bbox, first 500 in node order, existing
     facility nodes removed). The rebuild is verified: all ten sites arm C
     actually chose are members of this set. Only the SELECTION RULE differs, so a
     C-random-pool -> C gap is the optimiser's contribution and nothing else.

     Everything else is identical to arms B, C and C-random:
       * the same 36 real facilities at their real coordinates, expanded x1.5
       * the same ten new sites
       * the SAME per-site capacity vector, copied facility-for-facility from
         arm C's own file
       * the same total system capacity, 6,842
       * the same population, demographics, PM2.5 field, street network and
         opening dates, and every parameter below identical to arm C's file

     Site selection used python random.Random(6) - a FIXED, STATED site-seed,
     deliberately distinct from the bounding-box arm's site-seeds 1/2/3, and
     unrelated to randomSeed below, which is the model's own RNG seed exactly as
     in arms A/B/C.

     Built by scripts/build_scenario_crandom_pool_2026.py ->
     data/shelters/shelters_2026_random_sites_r6.csv (46 facilities, 6,842 spaces).

     Population n = 6842 is the 2025 Tri-County Point-in-Time count for
     Multnomah County (PSU HRAC, published 2025-11-04): 10,526 people
     experiencing homelessness, of whom more than 65% were unsheltered.
     The model represents the UNSHELTERED only.

     enableHeterogeneity=1        residents carry sourced age / sex / mobility /
                                  asthma / COPD attributes and walk at their own speed.
     respectShelterOpeningDates=1 shelters open on their real dates (A-02).

     walkingSpeedMps is declared but IGNORED when heterogeneity is on. -->
<sweep runs="1">
	<parameter name="numAgents" type="constant" constant_type="int" value="6842"/>
	<parameter name="randomSeed" type="constant" constant_type="int" value="44"/>
	<parameter name="minutesPerTick" type="constant" constant_type="number" value="1.0"/>
	<parameter name="walkingSpeedMps" type="constant" constant_type="number" value="1.30"/>
	<parameter name="shelterArrivalDistanceM" type="constant" constant_type="number" value="200.0"/>
	<parameter name="evacuationThresholdUgM3" type="constant" constant_type="number" value="55.5"/>
	<parameter name="simulationHours" type="constant" constant_type="int" value="312"/>
	<parameter name="scenarioCode" type="constant" constant_type="int" value="10"/>
	<parameter name="enableHeterogeneity" type="constant" constant_type="int" value="1"/>
	<parameter name="respectShelterOpeningDates" type="constant" constant_type="int" value="1"/>
</sweep>
